1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,200
This logo shouldn't be able to glow.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:06,080
After ten years, Apple brought it back on the new MacBook Pro.

3
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:08,520
But its OLED screen only makes light from the front.

4
00:00:08,760 --> 00:00:09,890
There's no light behind it.

5
00:00:10,390 --> 00:00:11,690
So where's the glow coming from?

6
00:00:11,930 --> 00:00:12,960
Let's open the lid.

7
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:16,030
Hidden behind the screen are four tiny LEDs.

8
00:00:16,270 --> 00:00:18,920
Apple says it built this light source just for the logo.

9
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:21,630
A mirror-like layer bounces their light,

10
00:00:21,870 --> 00:00:23,770
a frosted sheet spreads it out evenly,

11
00:00:24,010 --> 00:00:25,950
and it shines through the logo.

12
00:00:26,190 --> 00:00:27,290
No bright spots.

13
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:29,510
It glows whenever your Mac is awake.

14
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:32,150
Brighter in a bright room, dimmer in a dark one.

15
00:00:32,390 --> 00:00:32,980
Don't like it?

16
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:34,230
Apple lets you switch it off.

17
00:00:34,730 --> 00:00:35,800
Follow InvisiTech for more.

